Title

Demonstration of Strings in Arduino

Aim

To demonstrate String operations in Arduino.

Theory

Strings are used to store and manipulate text data. Arduino provides String functions such as length(), concatenation, and comparison.

Components Required
Arduino Uno
USB Cable
Computer/Laptop
Procedure
Connect Arduino Uno to the computer.
Open Arduino IDE.
Create a String variable.
Display the string using Serial Monitor.
Upload and execute the program.
Code
String name = "Arduino";

void setup()
{
  Serial.begin(9600);

  Serial.println(name);
  Serial.println(name.length());
}

void loop()
{
}
